mainmenu "AIFoundry Arduino emlearn sample"

config AIFOUNDRY_ARDUINO_LOOP_COUNT
	int "Number of loop() iterations before kernel exit"
	default 3
	help
	  Arduino's `loop()` is normally an infinite cycle.  The
	  ET-SoC1 launcher (basic_launcher) kills the kernel after
	  --kernel_launch_timeout seconds if it never returns, which
	  loses the exit code and can clip the trace ring.  This
	  caps the sketch's loop count so the kernel exits cleanly
	  via aifoundry_kernel_exit() — set to 0 to disable the cap
	  and let the sketch run forever.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
